{"title":"Distance formula","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>distance formula</b> is a direct application of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> in the setting of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_coordinate_system\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cartesian coordinate system\">Cartesian coordinate system</a>.  In the two-dimensional case, it says that the distance between two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">points</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16bee54a1399378afcb44e9055e6d98b308c23b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = (x_1, y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815b665e363b0d4d2e9376dca8d9a3adfbf5ecd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 = (x_2, y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba92279cdba4999cfcbde71d996166c341098aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\sqrt{(x_1 - x_2)^2 + (y_1 - y_2)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"230\" height=\"32\" />.  In the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-dimensional case, the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73b2fdc74153202689e66cb0fca0a5533067299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,...,a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f7068ddf35490a78f2ad9e8d5c4e92833bca8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_1,b_2,...,b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e61d4a805700f30d5befd7e50b70b2e14af074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a_1-b_1)^2+(a_2-b_2)^2+\\cdots+(a_n-b_n)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"337\" height=\"32\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Shortest_distance_from_a_point_to_a_line\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Shortest distance from a point to a line</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof_1_(Coordinate_Analysis)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 1 (Coordinate Analysis)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_2_(Vector_Projections)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 2 (Vector Projections)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof_3_(Area_&amp;_Determinant)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 3 (Area &amp; Determinant)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shortest_distance_from_a_point_to_a_line\">Shortest distance from a point to a line</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Shortest distance from a point to a line\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95c6e28cc1c980185c6fc988e3a8e4e01266ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa788076d50059891f89ee30b4343196d6939e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b41118918fc372f0e42b4dc38763977c0070d764.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=\\frac{|ax_1+by_1+c|}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}.\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Proof_1_.28Coordinate_Analysis.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_1_(Coordinate_Analysis)\">Proof 1 (Coordinate Analysis)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 1 (Coordinate Analysis)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6af3f87cd936b2b7be4a718c0886c8446c9c6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax + by + c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d5cee81e8668cf3ae1fbeacf75dc7aa2b30823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -\\dfrac{a}{b}x - \\dfrac{c}{b}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"34\" />\nThus, the perpendicular line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b354638f824de285dce6d6d3f72163cb287aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cecc79b1a474ef06f682423f36e8ff9fc5fbe45b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{x-x_1}{a}=\\dfrac{y-y_1}{b}=\\dfrac{t}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}},\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"41\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the parameter.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> will be the distance from the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b354638f824de285dce6d6d3f72163cb287aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> along the perpendicular line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2ccf383b37c445fd12553d8bfaccd183f5906ab8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = x_1 + a \\cdot \\dfrac{t}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/5224444e299ce9a363ac5decd92ea1816435ded5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = y_1 + b \\cdot \\dfrac{t}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}.\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>This meets the given line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95c6e28cc1c980185c6fc988e3a8e4e01266ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, where:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6ba4df459edd33f5fdf86d7825315d84f04f3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\left(x_1 + a \\cdot \\dfrac{t}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}\\right) + b\\left(y_1 + b \\cdot  \\dfrac{t}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}\\right) + c = 0\\]\" width=\"430\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/8077b2738403e402f33929e8c52c36ed245e5fb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies ax_1 + by_1 + c + \\dfrac{t(a^2+b^2)}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}} + c = 0\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b8865ab174fcca1ebe2f2bb8f77e6ce0df6136.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies ax_1 + by_1 + c + t \\cdot \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} = 0,\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5ce92e2fad16bfb9c26f893a47b2e0bdadfb3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t \\cdot \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} = -(ax_1+by_1+c)\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff5762ec41833ad9f00bd0f5161ac286ac30e98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies t = \\dfrac{-(ax_1+by_1+c)}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the perpendicular distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b354638f824de285dce6d6d3f72163cb287aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> to the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95c6e28cc1c980185c6fc988e3a8e4e01266ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81d96fbe201471396910b4ba2fb87e79601948b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = |t| = \\dfrac{|ax_1 + by_1 + c|}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}.\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Proof_2_.28Vector_Projections.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_2_(Vector_Projections)\">Proof 2 (Vector Projections)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 2 (Vector Projections)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>It is well known that the vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a3431f92dd2fa16897b8840216b047b014762e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf n = \\langle a,b\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> is normal to the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6af3f87cd936b2b7be4a718c0886c8446c9c6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax + by + c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />. Given the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43eb8aa9a09433f27bafc7f9cab02e9932c08a91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1, y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d7c5a5d81b236ccac6c42cf478f4a227c153f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x_2,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> is an arbitrary point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72d7f682b376fdfb6ae7c730f29c7609603708f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ\\not\\perp L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3ee34a8dc58e3d461cc9e07f7de08de887e17b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; import geometry; unitsize(1cm);  defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)); pen lineStyle = black + 0.8pt; pen vectorStyle = blue + 1pt; pen helperStyle = dashed + gray(0.4) + 0.6pt;  pair Q = (3, 3); pair dirL = unit((1, -0.6));  pair n = unit((-dirL.y, dirL.x));  pair L_start = Q - 3.5 * dirL; pair L_end = Q + 3.5 * dirL;  pair P = Q + 1.2 * dirL + 1.3 * n; pair QP = P - Q;  real proj_length = dot(QP, n); pair P_proj = Q + proj_length * n;  real n_length = 2.4;  pair N_end = Q + n_length * n;  draw(L_start--L_end, lineStyle); label(&quot;$L$&quot;, L_end, SE);  draw(rightanglemark(Q + dirL, Q, Q + n, 8));  draw(P--P_proj, helperStyle); draw(Q--P_proj, helperStyle);  draw(Q--N_end, vectorStyle, Arrow(4)); label(&quot;$\\mathbf{n}$&quot;, N_end, NE);  draw(Q--P, red + 1pt, Arrow(4));  dot(&quot;$Q(x_2, y_2)$&quot;, Q, SW); dot(&quot;$P(x_1, y_1)$&quot;, P, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"302\" height=\"215\" />\nThen, it is simple enough to visualize that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae5ad4d145d362751372082c9292b139ed45e9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\Big|\\mathrm{proj}_{\\textbf n}\\Big(\\overrightarrow{QP}\\Big)\\!\\Big| = \\frac{\\Big|\\overrightarrow{QP}\\cdot\\textbf n\\Big|}{|\\textbf n|}\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"57\" />\nWith <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99eed2e2546d83cfb08ed750a6c9992dedc67b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{QP} = \\langle x_1-x_2, y_1-y_2\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"25\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7740a542b08375eb66f3b24f9137df4495e700a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overrightarrow{QP}\\cdot\\textbf n = a(x_1 - x_2) + b(y_1 - y_2) = ax_1 + by_1 - (ax_2 + by_2)\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"26\" />\nand since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4d854203eb67e20146371579fe2e062ff5d853c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q\\in L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574cd26ba0fbfb46272d82eb95420c5fdbc53546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2, y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8a029bf523afac09183b5a26f9df9459aeb044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax_2 + by_2 = -c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff107348c22abade56ad63304b0bd0a164e27924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{QP}\\cdot\\textbf n = ax_1 + by_1 + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"24\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7ee27caa027dee8aa1a47288ba84ec5c53bea268.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{d = \\frac{\\big|ax_1 + by_1 + c\\big|}{\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}}}\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"57\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Proof_3_.28Area_.26_Determinant.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_3_(Area_&amp;_Determinant)\">Proof 3 (Area &amp; Determinant)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 3 (Area &amp; Determinant)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Alternately, one can connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />- &amp; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercepts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7ba20e5d05eef6b8dbca36a51491b43035b540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I\\left(0, -\\tfrac{c}{b}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"72\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/6590e43f2d8fa73a274ea13857c7fdfe42e92c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J\\left(-\\tfrac{c}{a}, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"75\" height=\"24\" />. This renders <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69dc6cb0433839898a4680f28a578515c2f3f22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PIJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127ba70f639f48b325137af63b7b0a9fc72fe953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IJ$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1d91fa5ba6fd015073530310bab5e40dcb350c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));  // 1. Define Constants for the lines and points // L: ax + by + c = 0. We&#39;ll use a=1, b=2, c=-6 which gives a downward slope (-1/2) // This puts I at (0, 3) and J at (6, 0). real a=1, b=2, c=-6; pair P = (3, 4); // Point P outside L  // Calculated Intercepts pair I = (0, -c/b); pair J = (-c/a, 0);  // 2. Setup Coordinate Axes pair O = (0,0); draw(O--(J.x + 1, 0), Arrow(4)); // X-axis draw(O--(0, I.y + 1), Arrow(4)); // Y-axis label(&quot;$x$&quot;, (J.x + 1, 0), E); label(&quot;$y$&quot;, (0, I.y + 1), N);  // 3. Define Line L and the altitude footprint // We use &#39;geometry&#39; package commands to precisely compute the perpendicular projection line lineL = line(I, J); line altLine = perpendicular(P, lineL); pair H = intersectionpoint(lineL, altLine); // H is the foot of the altitude  // 4. Draw Geometry draw(lineL, black + 0.8pt); // Draw line L draw(I--P--J, blue + 0.5pt); // Draw sides PI and PJ (pale for contrast)  // Draw the Altitude d draw(P--H, red + 1pt);   // Draw the right angle mark at H markscalefactor=0.15; // Set size of the right angle box draw(rightanglemark(P, H, J, 1)); // P-H-J is 90 degrees  // 5. Dots and Labels dot(&quot;$P(x_1,y_1)$&quot;, P, NE); dot(&quot;$I(0,-c/b)$&quot;, I, SW); dot(&quot;$J(-c/a,0)$&quot;, J, NE); dot(H); // H is implicitly defined by the altitude  // Labels label(&quot;$L$&quot;, (I+J)/2, SW, black); label(&quot;$d$&quot;, (P+H)/2, W, red); [/asy]\" width=\"592\" height=\"315\" />\nFundamentally, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69dc6cb0433839898a4680f28a578515c2f3f22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PIJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c2ed914a53f91e122c9de3ba861fe55a3e00ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle PIJ] = \\frac{1}{2}d\\cdot IJ = \\frac{d}{2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{c}{b}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{c}{a}\\right)^2} = \\frac{d}{2}\\left|\\frac{c}{ab}\\right|\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"43\" />\nOn the other, the same area can be expressed by evaluating the determinant of the 2x2 matrix of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5d6402e945c44113348fb0f372c3f490f8e0ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{IP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4107b249d14be64aad556b3063cb98642d5b798e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{IJ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"21\" />. Namely, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e900f57fd411ad53f9c0a9a638eca686a1544287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{IP} = \\left\\langle x_1, y_1 + \\tfrac{c}{b}\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"141\" height=\"27\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b101a5325fbd5799f6e0c272126e8e2b9bcbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{IJ} = \\left\\langle -\\tfrac{c}{a}, \\tfrac{c}{b}\\right\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"107\" height=\"27\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55790f3e58e5c1bdae940cc1a9e22634dd5fd2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle PIJ] = \\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\det\\!\\begin{bmatrix}x_1 &amp; -\\tfrac{c}{a} \\\\ y_1 + \\tfrac{c}{b} &amp; \\tfrac{c}{b}\\end{bmatrix}\\right| = \\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\frac{cx_1}{b} + \\frac{c}{a}\\left(y_1+\\frac{c}{b}\\right)\\right| = \\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\frac{c}{ab}\\right|\\big| ax_1 + by_1 + c\\big|\\]\" width=\"612\" height=\"44\" />\nEvidently, by equating the two expressions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe8a4951547636f9580755a8576159f0a9e8dee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle PIJ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0eaab09bd6e7af3b53800de7a20ea5be7e34ac6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} = \\big| ax_1 + by_1 + c\\big| \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\therefore d = \\frac{\\big| ax_1 + by_1 + c\\big|}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}}\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"57\" />\n~jxyrx\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082844\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 308/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 289/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15312/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.286      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    7.286      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4348:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082844 and revision id 288573. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}